                "paragraphs": [
                    {
                        "text": "I've been interested in computing since I was six, and I still haven't grown tired of it. Over the past ten years, I've worked across different areas: keeping computers running, helping users, looking after systems, and now mostly developing software.",
                        "emphasis": [
                            "ten years"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "I started as a systems administrator, mainly working with hardware and operations. I spent a lot of time with colleagues who simply used IT as a tool for their work. They taught me as much about communication as computers taught me about troubleshooting: how to ask the right questions, be patient, and explain a technical problem without expecting an IT background.",
                        "emphasis": [
                            "I started as a systems administrator"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "I then moved into IT support and product support, with L1–L3 support, system monitoring and on-call responsibilities. Along the way, I got to know enterprise environments in greater depth: servers, networks and enterprise resource planning systems. When something went wrong, understanding the whole operation mattered just as much as the part where the issue appeared.",
                        "emphasis": [
                            "IT support and product support"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "I've also gained experience in international projects and worked on assignment in Thailand. I hold an advanced English language exam qualification and have used English with colleagues abroad on real professional tasks.",
                        "emphasis": [
                            "experience in international projects"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "Later, software development became my main focus: I developed PHP applications, wrote reports and worked on database queries. I currently work as a mid-level Laravel developer, while also leading development at my own software business, SzoftLab.",
                        "emphasis": [
                            "software development became my main focus",
                            "SzoftLab"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "I still bring those earlier experiences into my work. When developing software, I also think about how a system will run in production and what it will be like for the people using it every day. I enjoy having something to think through and a problem to solve — and if I learn something new along the way, even better.",
                        "emphasis": []
                    }
                ]
